---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Cookie policy" description="What cookies and similar technologies this site uses, why, and how to control them.">
<div class="wrap"><Breadcrumbs trail={[{ label: 'Cookie policy', href: '/cookie-policy/' }]} /></div>
<section class="wrap" style="padding:1.5rem 1.25rem 0">
  <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
  <h1 style="max-width:22ch">Cookie policy</h1>
  <p style="max-width:46ch;font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:1.2rem 0 1.8rem">
    What is stored on your device when you read this site, what it is used for, and how to turn it
    off.
  </p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What a cookie is</h2>
    <p>
      A small text file placed on your device by a website. Similar technologies — local storage,
      pixels, tags — do comparable things and are covered by this policy wherever they are used.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site uses</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Strictly necessary</strong></td>
          <td>Security, load balancing and delivering pages. These cannot be switched off without breaking the site.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Consent record</strong></td>
          <td>Where a consent banner is shown, a record of your choice is stored so you are not asked on every page.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Analytics</strong></td>
          <td>Aggregate measurement of which pages are read. Used to decide what to write next, not to identify individuals.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Advertising</strong></td>
          <td>Where advertising is served by a third-party network, that network may set its own cookies. Those are governed by the network's policy, not this one.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Some cookies are set by companies other than us — an advertising network, an analytics provider,
      or an embedded service. We do not control what those companies do with the data they collect,
      and their own policies govern it. Where a link on this site is an affiliate link, following it
      may cause the destination site to set a cookie recording the referral; see the
      <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Where a consent mechanism is presented — for readers in regions whose law requires one — your
      choice is recorded and can be changed at any time through that mechanism.
    </p>
    <p>
      Independently of anything this site does, your browser can block or delete cookies. Every major
      browser has this in its settings, usually under privacy. Blocking strictly necessary cookies may
      stop parts of the site working.
    </p>

    <h2>How long cookies last</h2>
    <p>
      Some cookies are deleted the moment you close your browser; these are session cookies, and they
      generally exist to keep a page working while you are on it. Others persist for a set period so
      that a preference — a consent choice, for instance — does not have to be collected again on
      every visit. The retention period is set by whoever placed the cookie, which for third-party
      cookies means the third party rather than us.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not sell personal data, and it does not use cookies to build a profile of you for
      resale. Where advertising is served, the network's own targeting practices apply and are
      described in that network's policy — but the arrangement is that they serve advertising, not
      that we hand over a reader database.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy changes when what the site uses changes. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>
      covers personal data more broadly, and the <a href="/terms/">terms</a> cover use of the site.
    </p>

    <p class="note">
      {SITE.name} is an independent publication. If anything here is unclear, the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> is the route to a straight answer.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
